# Mandatory `/grill-me` (Strict)

**Do not guess requirements.** When anything is ambiguous, missing, or assumed, run `/grill-me` - do not proceed by filling gaps with assumptions.

## When `/grill-me` is required

Run it **before**:
- Writing or updating a feature specification
- Modifying architecture documents or ADRs in `docs/adr/`
- Breaking roadmap items into tickets in `.scratch/backend/issues/`
- Writing code for requirements that have ambiguous boundaries

## Core GaliGuide Grilling Topics
- Spatial boundary logic (e.g. radius search vs bounding box filtering)
- Privacy boundaries (phone consent, municipal ward lead role restrictions)
- Zero-cost mapping constraints (verifying no accidental Google Maps SDK calls)
- Bilingual Devanagari indexing and normalization
- Neon serverless connection limits and pooling strategies
